{
  "summary": "This experiment tested transformer aggregation in a high-performing multimodal setup (scvi_n200 RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l image encoder, concat fusion) compared to avgpool aggregation (config_008). Validation accuracy improved slightly to 0.7207 (from 0.7150), while validation F1 decreased marginally to 0.6815 (from 0.6872). The results suggest transformer aggregation may offer minimal accuracy gains but do not conclusively confirm its superiority over avgpool. Uncertainty remains about the optimal aggregation strategy and whether other design choices, such as fusion methods or encoder combinations, could further enhance performance."
}

